IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-procedure`

-- bgg4-tests-procedure: tests for Art 102 to 107.  Expected values are written from the text
-- (quoted beside the assertion), not from the code's output.

§ `Art 102 tests`

-- (1) "Soweit erforderlich stellt das Bundesgericht die Beschwerde der Vorinstanz sowie den allfälligen anderen Parteien, Beteiligten oder zur Beschwerde berechtigten Behörden zu und setzt ihnen Frist zur Einreichung einer Vernehmlassung an."
#ASSERT `Art 102(1) the Federal Supreme Court must serve the appeal and set a time limit for observations` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 102(1) the Federal Supreme Court must serve the appeal and set a time limit for observations` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 102(1) the Federal Supreme Court must serve the appeal and set a time limit for observations` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "Die Vorinstanz hat innert dieser Frist die Vorakten einzusenden." The time limit ends 20 April 2026.
#ASSERT `Art 102(2) the lower instance has sent the files within the time limit` (Date 20 4 2026) (Date 19 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 102(2) the lower instance has sent the files within the time limit` (Date 20 4 2026) (Date 20 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 102(2) the lower instance has sent the files within the time limit` (Date 20 4 2026) (Date 21 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) "Ein weiterer Schriftenwechsel findet in der Regel nicht statt."
#ASSERT `Art 102(3) a further exchange of submissions takes place` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 102(3) a further exchange of submissions takes place` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 103 tests`

-- (1) "Die Beschwerde hat in der Regel keine aufschiebende Wirkung."
#ASSERT `Art 103(1) the appeal has suspensive effect` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 103(1) the appeal has suspensive effect` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(a) "in Zivilsachen, wenn sie sich gegen ein Gestaltungsurteil richtet"
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(a) the appeal has suspensive effect in civil matters` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(a) the appeal has suspensive effect in civil matters` `appeal in civil matters` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(a) the appeal has suspensive effect in civil matters` `appeal in criminal matters` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(b) "in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen einen Entscheid richtet, der eine unbedingte Freiheitsstrafe oder eine freiheitsentziehende Massnahme ausspricht; die aufschiebende Wirkung erstreckt sich nicht auf den Entscheid über Zivilansprüche"
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(b) the appeal has suspensive effect in criminal matters` `appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(b) the appeal has suspensive effect in criminal matters` `appeal in criminal matters` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(b) the appeal has suspensive effect in criminal matters` `appeal in criminal matters` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(b) the appeal has suspensive effect in criminal matters` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(c) "in Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen, wenn sie sich gegen eine Schlussverfügung oder gegen jede andere Verfügung richtet, welche die Übermittlung von Auskünften aus dem Geheimbereich oder die Herausgabe von Gegenständen oder Vermögenswerten bewilligt"
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(c) the appeal has suspensive effect in international legal assistance in criminal matters` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(c) the appeal has suspensive effect in international legal assistance in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(c) the appeal has suspensive effect in international legal assistance in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(c) the appeal has suspensive effect in international legal assistance in criminal matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(d) "in Verfahren auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Amtshilfe in Steuersachen"
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(d) the appeal has suspensive effect in international administrative assistance in tax matters` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2)(d) the appeal has suspensive effect in international administrative assistance in tax matters` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) the paragraph: order is kind, formative, custodial, civil-claims part, legal assistance, final order, other order, tax assistance
#ASSERT `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` `appeal in criminal matters` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- civil matter, not a formative judgment: limb (a)'s "wenn" fails
#ASSERT `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` `appeal in civil matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- criminal matter, the part concerned is the decision on civil claims: the effect does not extend to it
#ASSERT `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` `appeal in criminal matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a public-law appeal outside the three fields: no limb reaches it
#ASSERT `Art 103(2) the appeal has suspensive effect to the extent of the claims` `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "Der Instruktionsrichter oder die Instruktionsrichterin kann über die aufschiebende Wirkung von Amtes wegen oder auf Antrag einer Partei eine andere Anordnung treffen."
#ASSERT `Art 103(3) the instructing judge may make a different order on suspensive effect` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 103(3) the instructing judge may make a different order on suspensive effect` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 103(3) the instructing judge may make a different order on suspensive effect` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) to (3) together: order, kind, formative, custodial, civil-claims part, legal assistance, final order, other order, tax assistance
-- the judge ordered suspensive effect in a case where the rule would give none
#ASSERT `Art 103 the appeal has suspensive effect` `the instructing judge ordered that the appeal has suspensive effect` `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the judge removed the effect that paragraph 2 gave
#ASSERT `Art 103 the appeal has suspensive effect` `the instructing judge ordered that the appeal has no suspensive effect` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no order, paragraph 2 gives the effect
#ASSERT `Art 103 the appeal has suspensive effect` `the instructing judge made no order on suspensive effect` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no order, no limb: the general rule of paragraph 1
#ASSERT `Art 103 the appeal has suspensive effect` `the instructing judge made no order on suspensive effect` `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no order, civil matter without a formative judgment
#ASSERT `Art 103 the appeal has suspensive effect` `the instructing judge made no order on suspensive effect` `appeal in civil matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Art 104 tests`

-- "Der Instruktionsrichter ... kann von Amtes wegen oder auf Antrag einer Partei vorsorgliche Massnahmen treffen, um den bestehenden Zustand zu erhalten oder bedrohte Interessen einstweilen sicherzustellen."
#ASSERT `Art 104 the instructing judge may order a provisional measure` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 104 the instructing judge may order a provisional measure` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 104 the instructing judge may order a provisional measure` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 105 tests`

-- (1) "Das Bundesgericht legt seinem Urteil den Sachverhalt zugrunde, den die Vorinstanz festgestellt hat."
#ASSERT `Art 105(1) the Court bases its judgment on the facts found by the lower instance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 105(1) the Court bases its judgment on the facts found by the lower instance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "Es kann die Sachverhaltsfeststellung der Vorinstanz von Amtes wegen berichtigen oder ergänzen, wenn sie offensichtlich unrichtig ist oder auf einer Rechtsverletzung im Sinne von Artikel 95 beruht."
#ASSERT `Art 105(2) the Court may correct or supplement the finding of the facts` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 105(2) the Court may correct or supplement the finding of the facts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 105(2) the Court may correct or supplement the finding of the facts` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "so ist das Bundesgericht nicht an die Sachverhaltsfeststellung der Vorinstanz gebunden"
#ASSERT `Art 105(3) the Court is bound by the finding of the facts` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 105(3) the Court is bound by the finding of the facts` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the paragraphs together: military or accident insurance, found by the lower instance, obviously wrong, violation
#ASSERT `Art 105 the Court is bound by the facts found by the lower instance` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 105 the Court is bound by the facts found by the lower instance` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 105 the Court is bound by the facts found by the lower instance` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 105 the Court is bound by the facts found by the lower instance` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 106 tests`

-- (1) "Das Bundesgericht wendet das Recht von Amtes wegen an."
#ASSERT `Art 106(1) the Court applies the rule of its own motion` `other law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 106(1) the Court applies the rule of its own motion` `fundamental rights` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) "Es prüft die Verletzung von Grundrechten und von kantonalem und interkantonalem Recht nur insofern, als eine solche Rüge in der Beschwerde vorgebracht und begründet worden ist."
#ASSERT `Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` `fundamental rights` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` `cantonal law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` `intercantonal law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` `fundamental rights` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` `cantonal law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` `intercantonal law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 106(2) the Court examines the violation` `other law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the paragraphs together
#ASSERT `Art 106 the Court examines the violation of the rule` `other law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 106 the Court examines the violation of the rule` `cantonal law` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 106 the Court examines the violation of the rule` `cantonal law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Art 107 tests`

-- (1) "Das Bundesgericht darf nicht über die Begehren der Parteien hinausgehen."
#ASSERT `Art 107(1) the Court is permitted to go beyond the claims of the parties` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) "Heisst das Bundesgericht die Beschwerde gut, so entscheidet es in der Sache selbst oder weist diese zu neuer Beurteilung an die Vorinstanz zurück. Es kann die Sache auch an die Behörde zurückweisen, die als erste Instanz entschieden hat."
#ASSERT `Art 107(2) the Court may give this outcome when it upholds the appeal` TRUE `the Court decides the matter itself` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 107(2) the Court may give this outcome when it upholds the appeal` TRUE `the Court remits the matter to the lower instance for a new judgment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 107(2) the Court may give this outcome when it upholds the appeal` TRUE `the Court remits the matter to the authority that decided as first instance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 107(2) the Court may give this outcome when it upholds the appeal` TRUE `another outcome` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 107(2) the Court may give this outcome when it upholds the appeal` FALSE `the Court decides the matter itself` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) first sentence: order is legal assistance, tax assistance, inadmissible, exchange took place, day exchange ended; 15 days after 10 March 2026 is 25 March 2026
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 25 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 25 3 2026)
-- over a month end: 15 days after 20 March 2026 is 4 April 2026
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 4 4 2026)
-- no exchange of submissions: the text gives no start
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- another field, or an appeal the Court does not consider inadmissible
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the last day for the decision not to enter` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) second sentence: "Auf dem Gebiet der internationalen Rechtshilfe in Strafsachen ist es nicht an diese Frist gebunden, wenn das Auslieferungsverfahren eine Person betrifft, gegen deren Asylgesuch noch kein rechtskräftiger Endentscheid vorliegt."
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the Court is bound by the period of 15 days` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- extradition with the asylum application finally decided: the exception is not made out and the first sentence's 15 days bind the Court
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the Court is bound by the period of 15 days` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the Court is bound by the period of 15 days` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) the decision is within 15 days: order legal assistance, tax assistance, inadmissible, exchange took place, day ended, asylum without final decision, day decided; last day 25 March 2026
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the decision not to enter is given within 15 days` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 24 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the decision not to enter is given within 15 days` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 25 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the decision not to enter is given within 15 days` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 26 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- tax assistance: the second sentence does not relieve the Court
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the decision not to enter is given within 15 days` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 26 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- extradition with an asylum application undecided: the Court is not bound by the period
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the decision not to enter is given within 15 days` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE (Date 26 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no exchange of submissions: no start day
#ASSERT `Art 107(3) the decision not to enter is given within 15 days` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE (Date 26 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) "entscheidet das Bundesgericht innerhalb eines Monats nach Anhebung der Beschwerde": brought 15 March 2026, one month later is 15 April 2026
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 4 2026)
-- brought 31 December 2026: 31 January 2027 exists
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` TRUE (Date 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2027)
-- brought 31 January 2026: February has no 31st, the text states no rule
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` TRUE (Date 31 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- brought 30 January 2026: February 2026 has no 30th either
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` TRUE (Date 30 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- brought 28 January 2026: 28 February 2026 exists
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` TRUE (Date 28 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- brought 29 January 2028 (a leap year): 29 February 2028 exists
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` TRUE (Date 29 1 2028) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2028)
-- not an appeal against a Patent Court licence decision
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the last day for the Court's decision on the licence appeal` FALSE (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Court decides: the day before, the day of, the day after 15 April 2026
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the Court decides within one month` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the Court decides within one month` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 15 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the Court decides within one month` TRUE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 16 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the Court decides within one month` TRUE (Date 31 1 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 107(4) the Court decides within one month` FALSE (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 14 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `The duties as regulative rules: traces (printed, not asserted)`

-- Art 102(1): no time limit; with no event the duty stands
#TRACE `Art 102(1) the Court's duty to serve the appeal and set a time limit` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Federal Supreme Court` DOES `serve the appeal and set a time limit for observations` AT 3
-- Art 102(2): a time limit of 10 days; files sent on day 10 and on day 11
#TRACE `Art 102(2) the lower instance's duty to send the files within the time limit` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Lower instance` DOES `send the files to the Federal Supreme Court` AT 10
#TRACE `Art 102(2) the lower instance's duty to send the files within the time limit` 10 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Lower instance` DOES `send the files to the Federal Supreme Court` AT 11
-- Art 107(3): 15 days
#TRACE `Art 107(3) the Court's duty to give the decision not to enter within 15 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Federal Supreme Court` DOES `give the decision not to enter on the appeal` AT 15
#TRACE `Art 107(3) the Court's duty to give the decision not to enter within 15 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Federal Supreme Court` DOES `give the decision not to enter on the appeal` AT 16
-- Art 107(4): one month, here 31 days (a month after 15 December)
#TRACE `Art 107(4) the Court's duty to decide within one month` 31 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Federal Supreme Court` DOES `decide on the appeal against the Federal Patent Court decision on a licence` AT 31
#TRACE `Art 107(4) the Court's duty to decide within one month` 31 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Federal Supreme Court` DOES `decide on the appeal against the Federal Patent Court decision on a licence` AT 32
